<div style="text-align: center;">
<p><strong>« <a href="/news-10-2020">October 2020</a> | <span style="text-decoration: underline;"><a class="newpage" href="/news-11-2020">November 2020</a></span> | <a class="newpage" href="/news-12-2020">December 2020</a> »</strong></p>
</div>



<p><span style="font-size:75%;">This is a series showing off news from the site, articles from the past month<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-1')">1</a></sup>, and fan-content for you to check out and discover! Be sure to leave a comment with your thoughts!</span></p>
<h4><span>Fandom Stuff</span></h4>
<ul>
<li>SCP-FR (French language branch of the SCP Foundation) is running <a href="http://fondationscp.wikidot.com/le-concours-des-404-ans">a contest</a> for the SCP-404-FR slot. Participants are asked to write about &quot;An error, something that caused one or the consequences of one&quot;. The visual design of the contest hub is worth checking out whether you speak French or not.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>SCP-EN (English, this wiki) is conducting another <a href="/instagram-fan-art-contest-fall-2020">Instagram Fan Art Contest</a>.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>SCP-PL (Polish) is running the inventive <a href="http://scp-pl.wikidot.com/rezurekcja-usunietych">Resurrecting The Deleted</a> contest. Participants pick a title of a work from the Deletions Log, and write an article using said title.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>SCP-KO (Korean) finished its latest <a href="http://ko.scp-wiki.net/bimonthly-contests-2020#toc4">bimonthly contest</a>. The theme of the contest was &quot;Language&quot;.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>SCP-DE (German) concluded its second <a href="http://scp-wiki-de.wikidot.com/halloween-wettbewerb-2020">Halloween contest</a>.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>SCP-IT (Italian) also ran a <a href="http://fondazionescp.wikidot.com/concorso-halloween-2020-dr-zeno">Halloween contest</a> this month.</li>
</ul>
<h4><span>Featured Articles</span></h4>
<ul>
<li><a href="/scp-5380">SCP-5380</a> (by chiifu): My World [Featured by Truc Linh and Quadraginta]<br />
<em>As a result, the entire mall was showered with snowflakes and small paper hearts.</em></li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li><a href="/the-significant-others-part-a">The Significant Others, Part &quot;A&quot;</a> by HarryBlank [Featured by weizhong, Grigori Karpin, and PlaguePJP]<br />
<em>&quot;I'm not a subject in containment,&quot; said Phil.</em><br />
<em>Azad grinned. &quot;Sure you're not.&quot;</em></li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li><a href="/deer-and-the-overseers">Deer And The Overseers</a> <tt>[Deer College]</tt> by stormbreath [Featured by The Pighead, Marcelles_Raynes, and Pedagon]<br />
<em>In honor of the termination of the old Council, I'll be looking at the history of Deer's interactions with them…</em></li>
</ul>
<h4><span>Reviewer's Spotlight Articles</span></h4>
<ul>
<li><a href="/scp-5462">SCP-5462</a> (Misery is the State of Every Soul Burdened by Mortality.) by Cerastes [Selected by Cerastes]<br />
<em>[…] commonly referred to as his Black Paintings due to their emotionally disturbing contents, themes, and use of dark colours.</em></li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li><a href="/scp-5456">SCP-5456</a> (Sweatmother) by faminepulse [Selected by Grigori Karpin]<br />
<em>“We can be human, yeah we can be respectful, but we can't tolerate chaos. You</em> have <em>to be our<sup>[sic]</sup> own dads.”</em></li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li><a href="/scp-4423">SCP-4423</a> (StepDemon) by Dyslexion [Selected by Sonderance]<br />
<em>SCP-4423 is a Tartarean-Class demonic entity that manifests during sleep paralysis.</em></li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li><a href="/scp-5788">SCP-5788</a> (Partners in sync) by Riemann [Selected by OCuin]<br />
<em>The integration of SCP-5788 into the plumbing of the kitchen makes removal and characterisation difficult.</em></li>
</ul>
